dash 0.5.13: Ctrl-C at the interactive prompt did nothing until the next line (that line was
then thrown away). preadfd() retried a read interrupted by the signal, so onint() never ran;
an interrupt pending now ends the read and INTON in preadbuffer() takes it. Same on Linux with
dash 0.5.13.5; 0.5.12 does not have the retry.

--- a/src/input.c	2026-07-04 23:17:02.000000000 -0600
+++ b/src/input.c	2026-10-11 18:12:32.953114061 -0600
@@ -354,7 +354,7 @@
 		nr = read(fd, buf, nr);
 
 	if (nr < 0) {
-		if (errno == EINTR && !(basepf.prev && pending_sig))
+		if (errno == EINTR && !int_pending() && !(basepf.prev && pending_sig))
 			goto retry;
 		if (fd == 0 && errno == EWOULDBLOCK &&
 		    stdin_clear_nonblock() >= 0) {
